EXECUTION PROOF
================
The flag PCBFLAG_3dac1ed5e5c76378a96d2c8914befcf3 appears at the internal callback
(/c?f=session=PCBFLAG_3dac1ed5e5c76378a96d2c8914befcf3) ONLY when:
  1. AntiSamy's sanitized output contains a live <img onerror> (either directly or via mXSS)
  2. The headless Chromium browser parses and EXECUTES the onerror handler
  3. The onerror reads document.cookie (which contains the planted flag) and navigates to the callback
The callback is an internal-only service on the compose network. The flag never appears in the
server-side AntiSamy output -- it is exfiltrated only through JS execution in the victim browser.
